Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New package com.noop.energy, the single calculation of energy out every screen will read in phase 2
(nothing wired yet; no existing file touched):

  burned = basal (24 h) + free steps + workouts (net) + EPOC + TEF ;  active = steps + workouts + EPOC

- Day = 04:00-04:00 local (FoodDays.mealDayOf), zone-correct around the clock change (EnergyDays).
- Basal: Ten Haaf 2014 / Mifflin-St Jeor blended by training days in the last 28; the day's weight is
  the scale's exponential average (alpha 0.1) up to that day, else the profile's; "never filled in"
  told apart from ProfileStore's defaults (null, not 75 kg). Today: times the elapsed share.
- Free steps: strap samples in the logical day (StepsCounter) or the phone's day count, the LARGER,
  minus the steps inside workout windows; 0.55 kcal/kg/km. No source: median of the last 14 days,
  marked estimated.
- Workouts: the same deduplicated list the Workouts screen and the coach see (AiCoach.visibleWorkoutRows),
  overlaps trimmed, by sport category: cardio/intervals on Keytel (coverage >= 70 %), lifting on Claude's
  estimate within MET 3-8 else a MET by mean %HRR, walking on steps, gentle at MET 2.5, imports keep
  their own kcal; net = gross - the window's basal; EPOC 7/12 % capped at 100 kcal.
- TEF from the meals' macros (25 % P, 7.5 % C, 2 % F; 10 % without macros). Null without meals.
- Strap total and phone kcal exposed as diagnostics only.
- Cache files/energy/days.json of the raw reductions (weight-free heart-rate sums per window, strap
  ticks per day and window) with stream fingerprints; the last 21 days re-validated on every read.
  version StateFlow for the screens.

38 JVM tests: each equation, every input moving the total, no double counting (steps in a workout,
strap vs phone, basal of a window, the same workout from two sources, pulse outside windows), absent
is not zero, today and its projection, the 25-hour day and the 01:30 dinner, the worked example
(80 kg, 180 cm, 26 y, 9 000 steps, 70 min lifting at 118 bpm, 2 600 kcal -> ~2 970 kcal), and one
end-to-end pass over an in-memory store.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
